cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "India AMR Trend Tracker: ICMR-AMRSN + NCDC NARS-Net"
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it, and also cite the underlying annual report — the ICMR-AMRSN or NCDC NARS-Net edition and table each value came from."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yashita
    family-names: Thakur
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7895-5250"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yashita-thakur/icmr-amr-tracker"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, reproducible pipeline that extracts national antimicrobial
  resistance surveillance results from the annual reports of both of India's
  national AMR surveillance networks — the Indian Council of Medical Research
  (ICMR) Antimicrobial Resistance Surveillance Network (AMRSN) and the National
  Centre for Disease Control (NCDC) National Antimicrobial Resistance
  Surveillance Network (NARS-Net) — and publishes them as structured, fully
  provenance-annotated data. Every extracted value carries the source report
  year and table number, enabling detection of cross-report revisions of the
  same underlying year. The two networks are published as parallel series and
  are never pooled: AMRSN reports percent susceptible and NARS-Net percent
  resistant, and because AMRSN publishes no percent intermediate for the
  organisms both networks report, an AMRSN percent resistant cannot be computed
  and the two series share no comparison value.
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - AMR
  - surveillance
  - India
  - ICMR
  - AMRSN
  - NCDC
  - NARS-Net
  - data extraction
  - open data
  - reproducible research
